 "Bug 1885702 - Fix initialization of masked text fragment in ClusterIterator.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D223050\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D225178", "files": ["layout/generic/nsTextFrame.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "109ce449c766690685f5996505c63af976521545", "parents": ["bf85012d1cd3a2b22a23265a259fde8076108052"], "tags": []}], "date": 1728563043, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "214": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1911948 - Don't let top-level multicol be paginated if it is inside a subdocument.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D218823\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D225210", "files": ["layout/generic/nsColumnSetFrame.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "d6d5e7b9b33656d1636e41cc435782d8dae29b41", "parents": ["109ce449c766690685f5996505c63af976521545"], "tags": []}], "date": 1728574398, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "215": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1913536 - Expose the special shorthands in the SpecifiedValueInfo for the CSS white-space shorthand.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D219426\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D225215", "files": ["devtools/server/tests/chrome/test_css-properties.html", "servo/components/style/properties/shorthands/inherited_text.mako.rs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "24e8110f76bdc628656066d666a81faf09feaa20", "parents": ["d6d5e7b9b33656d1636e41cc435782d8dae29b41"], "tags": []}], "date": 1728574450, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "216": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1911550 - Make text-transform:capitalize work even if no textrun is available, for \u003cselect\u003e intrinsic sizing.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D218533\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D225214", "files": ["dom/base/nsLineBreaker.cpp", "dom/base/nsLineBreaker.h", "layout/generic/nsTextRunTransformations.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3b741ac826fa658696dc64591548dc2bc2b66fb5", "parents": ["24e8110f76bdc628656066d666a81faf09feaa20"], "tags": []}], "date": 1728574645, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "217": {"changesets": [{"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1919212 - Only disable crash reporter in child process in test_duplex.cpp. r=pehrsons,cubeb-reviewers a=test-only\n\nDeath test work by forking. We want to disable the crash reporter only in the\nforked process.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D222468", "files": ["media/libcubeb/0002-disable-crash-reporter-death-test.patch", "media/libcubeb/test/test_duplex.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "38b558823a0f31c5f7525f809db566cca262277f", "parents": ["3b741ac826fa658696dc64591548dc2bc2b66fb5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1903259 - Simplify popupnotification markup. r=dao a=RyanVM\n\nI think this is preferable and seems to work.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D214875", "files": ["toolkit/content/widgets/popupnotification.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "094e2352170c634c81c00255599dd691c301190f", "parents": ["38b558823a0f31c5f7525f809db566cca262277f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1911948 - Add the testcase to WPT.  a=RyanVM\n\nWithout the patch, this fails with a timeout when it attempts to print.", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/break-inside-avoid-multicol-iframe-crash-print.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "7d5158c7c58bc96c53c3d1e5f7321a754ec2d172", "parents": ["094e2352170c634c81c00255599dd691c301190f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1914149 - Propagate zoom to new browsing contexts unconditionally. r=nika, a=RyanVM\n\nYour patch looks good to me. Not sure if there's a non-racy way of\ntesting the internal full-zoom value here...\n\nBut in general, assuming consistent zoom lacking other sources of\ninformation seems like the right thing to do.\n\nI agree that eventually we want to probably move the site-specific zoom\nimpl into Gecko (if only because Android is also going to want that, see\nbug 1547181, where I added a comment).\n\nCo-authored-by: Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D220277", "files": ["docshell/base/CanonicalBrowsingContext.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "88987a202bb22cfc038526aba60754098e205358", "parents": ["7d5158c7c58bc96c53c3d1e5f7321a754ec2d172"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1921797 - Check for degenerate ratio in nsCocoaUtis. r=mac-reviewers,mstange,bradwerth a=RyanVM\n\nThis is the straight-forward, uncontroversial fix, that can be uplifted.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D224211", "files": ["widget/cocoa/nsCocoaUtils.mm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "af87e14dc54de45ad2c956cc4e0a77541a8c12cf", "parents": ["88987a202bb22cfc038526aba60754098e205358"], "tags": []}], "date": 1728574704, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "218": {"changesets": [{"author": "longsonr \u003clongsonr@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1916111 - zoom polygons and polylines r=emilio, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D221079", "files": ["dom/svg/SVGPolyElement.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGPolygonElement.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGPolylineElement.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/svg-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/svg.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3ce142f981e4918b94fae8f89e99c42c2dafb83e", "parents": ["af87e14dc54de45ad2c956cc4e0a77541a8c12cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brad Werth \u003cbwerth@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1871557: Make CompositorThreadHolder::IsInCompositorThread more accurate. r=gfx-reviewers,aosmond a=RyanVM\n\nAs described in `CompositorThreadHolder::Shutdown`, it doesn't actually\nshutdown the compositor thread, and other work may still be running on\nit. Without this change, after calling `Shutdown`, `IsInCompositorThread`\nwill return false even for code running on the compositor thread. This\nchange adds an extra check that will return true if the current thread\nmatches the thread id of the compositor thread, even if the holder no\nlonger exists.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D221729", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorThread.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "05eb4518a7b11707dfe263a22d27cb6089b78f85", "parents": ["3ce142f981e4918b94fae8f89e99c42c2dafb83e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1728584325, "git_changesets": [null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "219": {"changesets": [{"author": "Daniel Holbert \u003cdholbert@cs.stanford.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1921128: Pixel-snap the contents of dialog boxes, to avoid arbitrary layout/clipping differences when viewport is even vs. odd pixel height.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D223797\n