ve portal login  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D220549\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D225963", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/captivePortal/browser.toml", "browser/base/content/test/captivePortal/browser_captivePortal_trr_mode3.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b2464648540936fa579c4b851423611a17206a01", "parents": ["bb8a21842c2e34c6e248c96f43b761eab067194c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1729169995, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "235": {"changesets": [{"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1920643 - Hook VariantClear to mitigate third-party crashes.  a=RyanVM\n\nFreeing the same BSTR twice is a recurring issue in third-party code\nthat affects our stability. By hooking VariantClear so that it cleans\nbstrVal, we can mitigate a subclass of these issues.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D223282\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D225922", "files": ["testing/cppunittest.toml", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/mozglue/WindowsOleAut32Initialization.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/mozglue/WindowsOleAut32Initialization.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/mozglue/moz.build", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/tests/TestDllInterceptor.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/tests/TestOleAut32Initialization.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/tests/moz.build", "toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "57d299c04606c2d47a3be8cbe2650823d418a805", "parents": ["b2464648540936fa579c4b851423611a17206a01"], "tags": []}], "date": 1729170046, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "236": {"changesets": [{"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1888494 - Make CanonicalBrowsingContext::FixupAndLoadURIString check set the correct TRR mode  a=RyanVM\n\nIt would seem sometimes in Firefox 77 we regressed the ability to set the TRR\nmode for a browsing context when opening a new tab.\nI confirmed that this bug didn't happen in Fx 77 when setting the\n`browser.tabs.documentchannel.parent-initiated` pref to `false`.\n\nThe nsIWebNavigation::LOAD_FLAGS_DISABLE_TRR is correctly passed into\nCanonicalBrowsingContext, but it doesn't end up getting used.\n\nThis sets the appropriate DefaultLoadFlags for BrowsingContext\nwhen the LOAD_FLAGS_DISABLE_TRR or LOAD_TRR_ONLY_MODE flags are present\nin nsDocShellLoadState::LoadFlags()\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D220550\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D225964", "files": ["docshell/base/BrowsingContext.cpp", "docshell/base/nsIWebNavigation.idl"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "6b7ed074fceeb2261dcea7a78357a5a855d1987f", "parents": ["57d299c04606c2d47a3be8cbe2650823d418a805"], "tags": []}], "date": 1729170357, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "237": {"changesets": [{"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1921022 - Run TestDllInterceptorCrossProcess and fix ccov TestDllInterceptor*. r=gstoll,win-reviewers a=test-only\n\nTestDllInterceptorCrossProcess is not listed in cppunittest.toml so not\nran. Also this test and TestDllInterceptor should be able to fully run\nunder ccov thanks to MOZ_NOPROFILE MOZ_NOINSTRUMENT (which is also now\nautomatically part of MOZ_NAKED).", "files": ["testing/cppunittest.toml", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/tests/AssemblyPayloads.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/tests/TestDllInterceptor.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/tests/TestDllInterceptorCrossProcess.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3e24a2eeee1ff21905a5c306298b839302e09748", "parents": ["6b7ed074fceeb2261dcea7a78357a5a855d1987f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan Varga \u003cjvarga@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "de